<title>CHILE: CMS, Nova in Chile gas deal-report.</title>
<headline>CMS, Nova in Chile gas deal-report.</headline>
<dateline>SANTIAGO 1996-09-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. company CMS Energy Corp and Canada's NOVA Corp have agreed to build a natural gas pipeline from northern Argentina to Chile to fuel Chile's booming mining industry, reported newspaper El Mercurio Monday.</p>
<p>The project, which will cost $700 million, will include building a pipeline across the Andes from Salta to Chile's Second Region and the construction of a 400 megawatt gas-fired power plant, said daily El Mercurio</p>
<p>Building work is due to start next year with the gas reaching Chile in early 1999, it said.</p>
<p>The project will be NOVA's second Chilean gas project -- the company is a partner in the GasAndes scheme to build a pipeline supply Santiago with gas from Mendoza in central Argentina.</p>
<p>--Margaret Orgill, Santiago newsroom, 562-699-5595x212</p>
